 "deviation_from_v1": "v1 (commit c3ab156) atom lines had two blanks after the 4-character name, shifting every fixed-column field by one; DISCUS 6.23.01 rejected the file at 'read stru' (error -49, 'File format specified as numbers only'), so the probe reported n[1]=0 and no data macro was run (evidence/20261028T232749Z_LAPTOP-NGU3BT0N). v2 writes DISCUS's own FORMAT 4 layout, checked by an emulation of read_atom_line against the DISCUS-written C1 file. Design, seeds, grid, oracle physics, predictions and thresholds are unchanged.",
 "deviation_from_v2": "v2 (commit ec703b4, run 20261028T234015Z_LAPTOP-NGU3BT0N) FAILED: DISCUS applied exp(-2*B*s^2) with B = 1.000 A^2 under 'temp use' although the files carry Biso = 0 (diagnosis: DIAGNOSIS_v2_RESULT.md). v3 changes ONLY the macros ('temp ignore' instead of 'temp use') and analyze.py (error-line regex no longer matches the start-up banner of asterisks, which made both L criteria fail on correct logs; new T criterion requires the log's 'Temp. factors' line to not say 'used'). Registered AFTER seeing v2 results. Seeds, grid, predictions, oracle and all numerical thresholds are unchanged, including the 1e-6 engine-precision limits.",
 "deviation_from_v3": "v3 (commit a243b4e, run 20261028T235829Z_LAPTOP-NGU3BT0N) FAILED 2/33: only B1 at engine precision (2e-5 vs 1e-6). Cause: 14/44 voxels on exact rounding ties s/0.001 = n + 1/2, where the engine and the NINT emulation pick different neighbouring table entries (RESULT_v3.md). Post hoc on v3 data, with the tie voxels taken from the matching candidate, total and diffuse agree to 2e-16 and 5e-15. v4 changes: (1) analyze.py declares the 216 tie voxels from the grid alone, requires the engine to equal one of the two candidate lookups there to 1e-12 (new R criteria), and completes the engine-precision oracle with that candidate; non-tie voxels are untouched; (2) FRESH seeds (block 20261101, random 20261102) so that the predictions are blind again, since the v3 realization has been seen. Registered after seeing v3. Grid, macros (apart from the structure they read), oracle physics and all numerical thresholds are unchanged.",
